<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kvarner Gulf</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gulf of Kvarner, Quarnero, Kvarner Bay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kvarner Gulf is a bay of the northern Adriatic Sea in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, between the Istrian peninsula and the mainland coast, with the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Rijeka</a> at its head. Its islands include Krk, Cres, Lošinj and Rab. In the 12th century its coastlands were part of the region called Merania, which gave its title to a line of German dukes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kvarner-gulf.jpg" alt="Kvarner Gulf" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of Peacekeeping Operations Cartographic Section · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kvarner_gulf_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
